{"content_hash": "0316ad582fef568e", "version_id": 593, "article_id": 60, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Indonesia frees 8 orangutans after Borneo fires", "title_zh": "印尼在婆罗洲火灾后放归8只红毛猩猩", "has_translation": true, "topic": "science", "source": "bbc_science", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c6073z5rvrk3o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1586778538929-ee34a8e9d8e7?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8d2F0Y2glMjBlbmRhbmdlcmVkJTIwb3Jhbmd1dGFuc3xlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNzY1NzczfDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Dan Dennis on Unsplash", "author": "Dan Dennis", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@cameramandan83?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/brown-monkey-on-brown-wooden-log-during-daytime-5ESfIy0yjZY?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(180, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(218, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SCIENCE", "seed": "459c4da79085"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 146, "reading_minutes": 0.7, "lead": "Eight orangutans have returned to the wild in Borneo. They were rescued from forest fires that destroyed their home. This is good news for a species in danger.", "lead_zh": "八只红毛猩猩已回到婆罗洲的野外。它们从摧毁其家园的森林大火中被救出。这对一个濒危物种来说是个好消息。", "preview": "On Friday, eight orangutans were released into a reserve in the west of Borneo. The group included three mothers, their three daughters, and", "preview_zh": "周五，八只红毛猩猩被放归到婆罗洲西部的一个保护区。这群猩猩包括三只母亲、她们的三只女儿和两只成年雄性。野生动物工作人员此前救出了它们。尽管这些动物感到紧张，但它们足够健康，可以回到森林。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 582, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/60/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 59.613, "size_bytes": 361440, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 167, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@f76eeb6/content/data/versions/593.json", "paragraphs": ["On Friday, eight orangutans were released into a reserve in the west of Borneo. The group included three mothers, their three daughters, and two adult males. Wildlife workers had rescued them earlier. Although the animals were stressed, they were healthy enough to go back to the forest.", "The fires started in August and September and burned large areas of the island. Because the flames moved quickly, many animals lost their homes. Indonesian wildlife authorities rescued 46 orangutans in total. However, only eight were ready to return to the wild on Friday. The others are still recovering.", "Orangutans are critically endangered, which means they face a very high risk of dying out. If people continue to cut down forests, these animals will have nowhere to live. Conservation groups say the rescue and release give hope. They also warn that more work is needed to protect the species."], "paragraphs_zh": ["周五，八只红毛猩猩被放归到婆罗洲西部的一个保护区。这群猩猩包括三只母亲、她们的三只女儿和两只成年雄性。野生动物工作人员此前救出了它们。尽管这些动物感到紧张，但它们足够健康，可以回到森林。", "火灾发生在八月和九月，烧毁了岛上大片地区。因为火势蔓延很快，许多动物失去了家园。印尼野生动物部门总共救出了46只红毛猩猩。然而，只有八只准备好在周五放归野外。其他猩猩仍在康复中。", "红毛猩猩属于极度濒危物种，这意味着它们面临极高的灭绝风险。如果人们继续砍伐森林，这些动物将无处可住。保护组织表示，这次救援和放归带来了希望。他们也警告说，还需要做更多工作来保护这个物种。"], "body": "On Friday, eight orangutans were released into a reserve in the west of Borneo. The group included three mothers, their three daughters, and two adult males. Wildlife workers had rescued them earlier. Although the animals were stressed, they were healthy enough to go back to the forest.\n\nThe fires started in August and September and burned large areas of the island. Because the flames moved quickly, many animals lost their homes. Indonesian wildlife authorities rescued 46 orangutans in total. However, only eight were ready to return to the wild on Friday. The others are still recovering.\n\nOrangutans are critically endangered, which means they face a very high risk of dying out. If people continue to cut down forests, these animals will have nowhere to live. Conservation groups say the rescue and release give hope. They also warn that more work is needed to protect the species.", "body_zh": "周五，八只红毛猩猩被放归到婆罗洲西部的一个保护区。这群猩猩包括三只母亲、她们的三只女儿和两只成年雄性。野生动物工作人员此前救出了它们。尽管这些动物感到紧张，但它们足够健康，可以回到森林。\n\n火灾发生在八月和九月，烧毁了岛上大片地区。因为火势蔓延很快，许多动物失去了家园。印尼野生动物部门总共救出了46只红毛猩猩。然而，只有八只准备好在周五放归野外。其他猩猩仍在康复中。\n\n红毛猩猩属于极度濒危物种，这意味着它们面临极高的灭绝风险。如果人们继续砍伐森林，这些动物将无处可住。保护组织表示，这次救援和放归带来了希望。他们也警告说，还需要做更多工作来保护这个物种。", "text": "On Friday, eight orangutans were released into a reserve in the west of Borneo. The group included three mothers, their three daughters, and two adult males. Wildlife workers had rescued them earlier. Although the animals were stressed, they were healthy enough to go back to the forest. The fires started in August and September and burned large areas of the island. Because the flames moved quickly, many animals lost their homes. Indonesian wildlife authorities rescued 46 orangutans in total. However, only eight were ready to return to the wild on Friday. The others are still recovering. Orangutans are critically endangered, which means they face a very high risk of dying out. If people continue to cut down forests, these animals will have nowhere to live. Conservation groups say the rescue and release give hope. They also warn that more work is needed to protect the species.", "vocab": [{"word": "endangered", "pos": "adj", "zh": "濒危的", "note": "常与 critically 连用，表示极度濒危", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "reserve", "pos": "noun", "zh": "保护区", "note": "指为保护动物而设立的区域", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "release", "pos": "verb", "zh": "放归，释放", "note": "常与 into the wild 搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rescue", "pos": "verb", "zh": "营救", "note": "强调从危险中救出", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "wildfire", "pos": "noun", "zh": "野火，山火", "note": "指难以控制的森林大火", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "habitat", "pos": "noun", "zh": "栖息地", "note": "动物自然生活和生长的地方", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "authority", "pos": "noun", "zh": "当局，官方", "note": "常用复数 authorities 指政府部门", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "recover", "pos": "verb", "zh": "恢复，康复", "note": "指健康或状态回到正常", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "conservation", "pos": "noun", "zh": "保护（环境）", "note": "常与 group 或 effort 搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "species", "pos": "noun", "zh": "物种", "note": "单复数同形", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Watch: Endangered orangutans released back into the wild after Borneo fires", "summary_original": "The critically endangered apes were rescued from intense wildfires that destroyed their habitat in August and September.", "body_original": "Watch: Endangered orangutans released back into the wild after Borneo fires\nTo play this video you need to enable JavaScript in your browser.\nThis video can not be played\nWatch: Endangered orangutans released back into the wild after Borneo fires\nClose\nEight orangutans have been released into the wild in Borneo after being rescued from intense wildfires.\nThree mothers, their three daughters and two adult males were freed in a reserve in the west of the island on Friday.\nIndonesian wildlife authorities rescued 46 of the apes, which are critically endangered, before fires tore through their habitat in August and September.\nRead more on this story.\nSubsection\nAsia\nPublished\n50 minutes ago\nShare\nclose panel\nShare page\nCopy link\nAbout sharing\nRelated topics\nIndonesia\nFollow\nIndonesia\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nIndonesia\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nOrangutans\nFollow\nOrangutans\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nOrangutans\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nBorneo\nFollow\nBorneo\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nBorneo\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a c